# A Windows path gets the path help even when one of its escapes (`\n`) happens to be valid.
mode: syntax
---- query
'C:\data\new.csv' | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..27
  PIPELINE@0..26
    LITERAL@0..17
      STRING@0..17 "'C:\\data\\new.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    TAKE_OP@20..26
      IDENT@20..24 "take"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      LITERAL@25..26
        LONG@25..26 "1"
  WHITESPACE@26..27 "\n"

error[DS0005]: unknown escape sequence `\d`
  --> query:1:4
  |
1 | 'C:\data\new.csv' | take 1
  |    ^^ not a valid escape
  |
  = help: if this is a Windows path, use a verbatim string `@'C:\data\new.csv'` or forward slashes `'C:/data/new.csv'`
  = note: valid escapes are `\\`, `\"`, `\'`, `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0` and `\u{...}`
